# 🎯 Interview Questions

### Q1. What is Leaderless Replication?

A replication model where **there is no primary/leader**. Any replica can accept reads and writes, and replicas synchronize later to achieve eventual consistency.

---

### Q2. Why do we need Version Numbers or Version Vectors?

To determine **which copy of the data is newer** and detect stale replicas during synchronization.

---

### Q3. What is Read Repair?

If a read detects that one replica has **stale data**, the system immediately writes the latest value back to that stale replica.

---

### Q4. What is Anti-Entropy?

A **background synchronization process** that continuously compares replicas and repairs differences, even if no client is reading the data.

---

### Q5. What is a Merkle Tree?

A hash-based tree used to **efficiently compare large datasets**. Instead of scanning every row, it compares hashes and drills down only into branches where differences exist.

---

### Q6. Why use Merkle Trees instead of comparing every row?

Because if most data is already identical, comparing hashes lets us skip entire matching subtrees, making synchronization much faster.

